    <LangVersion>7.3</LangVersion>
    <CodeAnalysisRuleSet>GW2CraftingHelper.ruleset</CodeAnalysisRuleSet>
    <!-- The warning ratchet. Every warning is an error; the StyleCop rules
         still outstanding are listed in NoWarn, so the build is green today and
         a NEW warning of any kind - compiler or a StyleCop rule already cleaned
         to zero - fails it.

         Why this shape rather than gating the CS prefix alone: measured against
         this project, csc honours WarningsAsErrors only for explicit codes.
         <WarningsAsErrors>CS</WarningsAsErrors> was tried first, with a CS0108
         deliberately reintroduced, and the build stayed green at 0 errors -
         i.e. the prefix form would have installed a gate that gated nothing.
         The same test with <WarningsAsErrors>CS0108</WarningsAsErrors> failed
         the build, which is how the prefix was ruled out rather than assumed.

         Before the ratchet, nine genuine compiler warnings had been sitting
         unread inside 2,723: a CS0108 field hiding Control.BackgroundColor on a
         Blish control subclass, and eight CS0649 on reflection-assigned DTO
         fields. Both are fixed at the source; nothing here suppresses a CS code.

         Each NoWarn entry is a bounded cleanup job, not a verdict. Removing one
         is a self-contained commit: fix that rule's sites, delete the ID, and
         the build proves the rule is clean and keeps it that way. The list only
         ever shrinks. Counts as of this commit are in CONTRIBUTING.md.

         SA1501 and SA1503 come out together or not at all. SA1501 (statement on
         a single line) stays silent while SA1503 (braces omitted) is live and
         takes over the same code the moment SA1503 is suppressed - measured
         here: SA1503 live reports 395 and SA1501 zero, SA1503 in NoWarn reports
         SA1501 394. Dropping SA1503 alone therefore turns 394 errors on, not
         off. Bracing a statement satisfies both, so the fix that clears one
         clears the other. -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <NoWarn>SA1005;SA1009;SA1025;SA1111;SA1114;SA1116;SA1117;SA1118;SA1119;SA1120;SA1122;SA1127;SA1128;SA1201;SA1202;SA1203;SA1204;SA1208;SA1210;SA1214;SA1310;SA1312;SA1401;SA1402;SA1407;SA1413;SA1500;SA1501;SA1502;SA1503;SA1505;SA1507;SA1508;SA1512;SA1513;SA1515;SA1516;SA1649</NoWarn>
